Cause: launchers created an owned run before the GUI wrote its active marker, allowing another installer process to purge an in-progress download. Fix: both launchers reserve the run before network I/O; GUI adoption securely replaces the launcher marker, with a bounded 10-minute handoff grace after launcher exit. Proof: npm run test:installer (8 frontend tests, 53 Rust passed/2 ignored, boundary/security tests passed); node --test scripts/installers-security.test.mjs (6 passed); bash scripts/test-install-sh.sh; installer cargo clippy -D warnings and fmt check.
